Amethyst: call -[NSView setWantsBestResolutionOpenGLSurface:] directly.

Upstream (HiDPI support, added 2013-11-11) invoked it through performSelector:withObject:YES so
it would compile on pre-10.7 SDKs. That passes a BOOL where an object is expected, which modern
clang rejects (-Wint-conversion is an error) and which only worked by calling-convention accident.
The method exists on every supported macOS (10.7+), so call it directly. Behaviour is unchanged:
it still runs only when LWJGL enables high-DPI mode (Retina) for the window.

Applies to: 2.9.1-nightly-20131120, 2.9.1, 2.9.2-nightly-20140822.

--- a/src/native/macosx/org_lwjgl_opengl_Display.m
+++ b/src/native/macosx/org_lwjgl_opengl_Display.m
@@ -78,8 +78,7 @@
 	[window_info->view setParent:window_info];
 	
 	if (window_info->enableHighDPI) {
-		// call method using runtime selector as its a 10.7+ api and allows compiling on older SDK's
-		[window_info->view performSelector:NSSelectorFromString(@"setWantsBestResolutionOpenGLSurface:") withObject:YES];
+		[window_info->view setWantsBestResolutionOpenGLSurface:YES];
 	}
 	
 	// set nsapp delegate for catching app quit events
